E["subzone:valley-of-bones"] = {t="subzone",n="Valley of Bones",z="shendralas",s="In Shen'dralas, the Valley of Bones lies choked with dust and ancient remains. Restless dead haunt its canyon, where centaur necromancers patrol among the colossal ribs of two Dead Goliaths.",h="In Shen'dralas, the Valley of Bones lies choked with dust and ancient remains.",sec={{t="A Canyon of the Restless Dead",b="Skeletal horrors walk the dusty ravines of the Valley of Bones, a canyon in the south. Centaur necromancers raise them with dark sorcery and command them. The spirits of the Magram centaur clan wander there too, bound to the barren earth long after their violent deaths. Two immense skeletons, called the Dead Goliaths, slump against the rocky cliffs. Scholars and travelers do not know where they came from.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Dead Goliaths?",a="The Dead Goliaths are the colossal remains of two unknown creatures against the canyon walls. Little is known of their kind or when they died, though their great size suggests beasts from a forgotten era.",al={"giant bones","huge skeletons desolace","dead goliaths lore"}},{q="Why are there centaur ghosts here?",a="The ghosts belong to the Magram, a violent centaur clan native to these arid plains. Unending war between centaur clans and the necromancers' meddling with the dead have denied the Magram spirits rest. They wander the canyon as apparitions.",al={"magram ghosts","why centaur spirits","undead centaur"}},{q="Who controls the skeletons in the valley?",a="Centaur necromancers practice dark rites in the canyon. They raise skeletal servants and command them to guard the crags and hold their ground among the dead.",al={"who commands skeletons","necromancers valley of bones"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you witness the valley's desecration of spirits. Dark practitioners bind Magram souls and raise twisted skeletal servants, perverting death's natural passage."},kw={"centaur","dead goliaths","magram","necromancers","shen'dralas","skeletons","valley of bones"},rel={"zone:shendralas","zone:desolace","topic:centaur"},src={"Valley of Bones"}}
E["zone:shendralas"] = {t="zone",n="Shen'dralas",z="shendralas",s="Centaur, outcasts, and quilboar contest Shen'dralas, south east of desolace. Ancient ruins rise among its crags, between Feralas and Mulgore.",h="Centaur, outcasts, and quilboar contest Shen'dralas, south east of desolace.",sec={{t="A Borderland in Turmoil",b="Shen'dralas lies in the heights south east of desolace, between Mulgore and Feralas. Its craggy passes and hidden enclaves shelter groups struggling to survive far from the great faction capitals. At Evenshade Overlook, some watch from secluded heights. At Outcast Hideaway, others seek refuge where they can be forgotten.",sp=0},{t="Centaur, Quilboar, and Ancient Ruins",b="Ancient ruins recall the highborne legacy behind Shen'dralas's name, yet the land is far from peaceful. Centaur feuds spill across the Magram Front, keeping old bloodshed alive along the borders. Bristleback quilboar hold fortified ground at Bristleback Retreat. Travelers find contested territory in the ravines.",sp=0},{t="The Valley of Bones",b="The valley of bones leads north-west toward Desolace and offers the main overland route into Shen'dralas. Sun and wind have bleached the passage. Its bones recall the violent struggles that still sweep through these crags.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Shen'dralas located?",a="Shen'dralas lies south east of Desolace, between Feralas and Mulgore. Travelers on foot usually enter from Desolace through the Valley of Bones.",al={"where is shendralas","shendralas location","how to get to shendralas"}},{q="Is Shen'dralas controlled by the Alliance or the Horde?",a="Neither the Alliance nor the Horde holds Shen'dralas. Roving centaur, hostile quilboar, outcasts, and isolated encampments make it a contested frontier.",al={"is shendralas horde","is shendralas alliance","who owns shendralas"}},{q="What major settlements or landmarks are here?",a="The main landmarks are the Valley of Bones, Bristleback Retreat, Evenshade Overlook, the Magram Front, Outcast Hideaway, and Shen'dralas's central expanse.",al={"shendralas subzones","landmarks in shendralas","points of interest shendralas"}},{q="Why are there centaur here?",a="Centaur territorial wars reach from Desolace's plains into Shen'dralas along the Magram Front. There, the clan clashes with local defenders and rival factions.",al={"centaur in shendralas","magram front","why are magram here"}},{q="What is Bristleback Retreat?",a="Bristleback Retreat is a fortified outpost held by Bristleback quilboar. They have secured a fierce foothold along the zone's edges.",al={"bristleback retreat","quilboar in shendralas"}},{q="What is the connection between this zone and Lake Dumont?",a="There is no known connection. Shen'dralas has its own landmarks, such as the Valley of Bones and Outcast Hideaway.",al={"lake dumont","shendralas map history"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, Shen'dralas's name recalls the ancient Highborne lore of Eldre'Thalas. Sentinels wary of reckless arcana in southern Kalimdor watch with interest.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, Shen'dralas borders Mulgore and Desolace. Quilboar and centaur aggression along its ridges threatens nearby ancestral hunting grounds.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you cross a remote, contested wilderness with alternate routes between Feralas and central Kalimdor. Travel calls for keen vigilance.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you find Shen'dralas just beyond Mulgore's southern reaches. Keeping the Magram and quilboar contained there helps protect Horde frontiers."},kw={"bristleback retreat","desolace","evenshade overlook","feralas","lake dumont","magram front","mulgore","outcast hideaway","shendralas","Valley of Bones"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-bones","zone:desolace","zone:feralas","zone:mulgore"},src={"Shen'dralas"}}
